    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d240">

                <pb facs="0584" n="488" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg488"/>

                <head>No. 218.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Edward
                            Thornton to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-03-25"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 25, 1879</date>.
                        (Received March 26.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I
                    forwarded to the governor-general of Canada copy of the note which was addressed
                    to me by Mr. Seward <pb facs="0585" n="489" xml:id="pg489"/> on the 13th ultimo,
                    relating to a concentration of Indians from British Territory in Bear Paw
                    Mountains.</p>
                <p>In reply, his excellency has transmitted to me for the information of the
                    Government of the United States copy of a report of a committee of the privy
                    council of Canada, appointed by him on the 17th instant, accompanied by a
                    memorandum upon the subject signed by the Canadian minister of the interior,
                    copy of which two documents I have the honor to inclose.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EDW’D THORNTON.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d240-a1.xml" xpointer="d240-a1"/>
